; Start AmiGTA with the stack it needs.
;
; RUN THIS FROM THE GAME'S OWN DRAWER:
;
;     cd DH1:Games/AmiGTA
;     execute run
;
; There is nothing to assign. The game finds its data through PROGDIR:, the
; drawer the executable itself was loaded from, so it works wherever you put
; it. Up to v0.0.1 every path was hard-coded to Work: and the README had to
; explain an assign; that is gone.
;
; THE LOOP IS FOR THE TEST RIG, and it costs a player nothing. When the game
; finds Work:reload.txt it deletes it and exits with return code 5 (WARN), and
; this script starts it again - with whatever binary and scripts are in the
; drawer NOW. That is how a build gets tested without the emulator being
; restarted: restarting WinUAE takes the keyboard and the mouse away from
; whoever is working at the same machine, every single time. A normal exit
; (ESC) returns 0 and falls out of the loop.
Stack 1000000
lab again
AmiGTA >gta.log
if warn
  skip again back
endif
